    <string name="macro_help_title">Macro instructions</string>
    <string name="macro_help_message">Macros automatically send a sequence of commands after an SPP device is connected. Put one command on each line. Command names are case-insensitive.\n\nTEXT &lt;text&gt;\nSends text using the current device encoding and transmit framing settings. Example: TEXT AT. Content is required. CRLF, LF, CR, or a custom delimiter is appended automatically when that framing mode is selected.\n\nHEX &lt;hex bytes&gt;\nSends raw bytes. Example: HEX 01 03 00 00 00 02 C4 0B. Spaces are optional, but the value must contain complete two-digit hexadecimal bytes.\n\nDELAY &lt;milliseconds&gt;\nWaits before running the next command. Example: DELAY 500. The allowed range is 0 to 60000 milliseconds.\n\n# &lt;comment&gt;\nA line beginning with # is documentation only and is ignored. Blank lines are also ignored.\n\nRepeat count\nRepeats the entire script from 1 to 100 times.\n\nHow to use\n1. Connect an SPP device in the app.\n2. Enter a macro name, script, and repeat count.\n3. Tap Save.\n4. Select the macro and tap Run. Macros are stored separately for each device address.\n\nExample\n# Query device status\nTEXT AT\nDELAY 500\nTEXT AT+VERSION?\n\nNote: macros currently do not support variables, conditions, or branching based on device responses.</string>
